00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.710 align:start position:0%
 
jack ma is one of the few entrepreneurs  in the world who have been able to  create over 1 trillion worth of value in  the marketplace last year in october of  2020 jack's companies were valued at a  total of 1.326 trillion dollars but  within just eight months his empire  shrunk to 696 billion dollars meaning  that he shed 630 billion dollars in  eight months that's the same as 78  billion dollars per month since then  things have only gotten worse as alibaba  has shed another 150 billion dollars in  the past four months putting jack's  total market cap loss at 780 billion  dollars  so what in the world happened to jack  maw  one year ago jack was killing it he was  the richest man in china he was a  massive celebrity and he was about to  conduct the world's largest public  offering with this finance company the  ant group but all of this would change  overnight on october 24th 2020 jack gave  a speech preceding the ipo of the ant  group he shared his thoughts on the  future of fintech along with a bit of  criticism of the chinese financial  system jack said quote we cannot  regulate the future with yesterday's  means there's no systemic financial  risks in china because there's no  financial system in china the risks are  a lack of systems now to most of us this  wouldn't seem like a big deal compared  to the things americans say about joe  biden and donald trump jack's remarks  are baby talk but the chinese government  would beg to differ  nowadays given the rapid financial and  technological advancements in china many  of us consider china to be a rapidly  developing country if not a developed  country i mean in terms of gdp the  general consensus is that china  overtaking the us is just a matter of  when not if so you would think that  china's political system is also quite  advanced but this is not the case  at all  you see the chinese government is run by  the ccp or the chinese communist party  and this isn't just for show either they  strongly believe in communist ideologies  and principles the reason that they  embraced a capitalistic economy is  because they realized that they couldn't  keep up with western countries without  capitalism but don't let that fool you  the ccp keeps a close eye on the free  market and they shut down anything and  everything that they consider a threat  jack's statement in october was a red  flag that the ccp had given jack way too  much freedom and they decided that it  was time to put him and all of his  billionaire friends in their place about  a week later on november 2nd jack was  invited to a closed door meeting with  chinese financial regulators at the time  this just seemed like a formality the  ant group was about to go public and the  meeting was presumably about the ipo the  next day though it would become clear  that the meeting was not so benign ant  group announced that they would be  canceling the ipo and that they would be  returning funds to investors who had  front randy ipo the wall street journal  later revealed that jack offered a  portion of the company to the ccp to  keep as long as they wanted but the ccp  declined its offer and all of this was  just the beginning after the ipo  cancellation the ccp began to crack down  on the ant group with regulation the ant  group was ordered to create a subsidiary  holding company that followed the rules  of the banking industry this way china's  massive state-owned banks could purchase  stakes in the subsidiary group the ccp  also targeted the and group's greatest  asset which was their consumer data the  ant group had gathered financial data on  billions of consumers throughout the  company's history and this was one of  their key competitive advantages the ccp  branded this data as a monopoly on  information and forced the ant group to  share this data with the rest of the  chinese financial industry while the ant  group was bending to the ccp's every  wish jack ma had disappeared he didn't  make any public appearances or speeches  he completely stopped tweeting in fact  he hasn't tweeted to this day and the  jack would miss the finals of his own  talent show where he was a judge there  is a lot of speculation that jack was  brought into custody and given a shakeup  during this time period but there's no  concrete proof thus far  moving back to the ant group the ccp  continued their demolition of the once  thriving fintech company one of the  crown jewels of the ant group was their  money market fund which was at one point  the largest in the world the ccp had  already been stifling the fund for a few  years at this point but this time they  didn't even have to do anything all of  the regulation the ccp forced onto the  ant group understandably spooked  investors of the fund and they would  leave in droves in the first quarter of  2021 the fund shrunk 18 to just under 1  trillion yuan  this adds up to almost a 50 decline from  the peak of the fund at the end of 2017.  on the bright side jack finally  resurfaced into the public's view in  early february  jack was spotted playing golf at the sun  valley golf resort and with that the ccp  decided to momentarily leave the ant  group and jack ma alone and move on to  jack's other assets in april the ccp hit  alibaba with a record 2.8 billion  anti-trust fine  apparently alibaba had eliminated and  restricted competition within the online  retailing space now i actually think  there's a bit of truth here as alibaba  is arguably a monopoly just like amazon  but alibaba's dominance hasn't really  changed over the past several years so  this is clearly just another hit on jack  alibaba put out a statement shortly  after that they would quote ensure its  compliance with the determination moving  forward the ccp took aim at alibaba's  web browser called the uc browser uc  browser was the second most popular  browser in china with over 400 million  active users only beat now by chrome in  march the ccp went ahead and removed the  app from the app store they didn't  provide any reasons as to why or give  any warning they straight up just  deleted the app to make things worse  jack's actions didn't just screw over  himself but also most chinese tech  companies the ccp was enacting very  similar punishments to all tech  billionaires in the country take diddy  for instance diddy is basically the  chinese uber and they have major players  backing them including apple tension and  uber the company was planning an ipo  during the summer and though the ccp  didn't block the ipo blocking the ipo  would have likely been the better  outcome for diddy  instead the ccp let diddy have their ipo  and right after the company went public  they announced the cyber security probe  into ditty they ordered diddy to not  accept any new customers and they  deleted the app from the app store let's  just say diddy's ipo didn't go too well  anyway moving back to jack ma on top of  the ccp tearing down his companies the  americans would decide that they wanted  to jump in on the fun as well  for years the sec has been trying to  crack down on chinese companies by  forcing regular american audits you see  almost every year one or two fraudulent  chinese companies make their way onto  the american stock market and cause  american investors to lose billions the  sec believes that imposing audits could  catch these frauds early on and save  investors from getting scammed  personally i think this is a serious  concern that does need to be addressed  but unfortunately for jag this couldn't  have taken place at a worse time at the  end of 2020 and the beginning of 2021  the sec really increased the pressure on  chinese companies they basically made an  ultimatum that they were going to d-list  chinese companies from the u.s stock  market if they didn't comply with sec  auditing the ccp of course refused to  cooperate the sec did give chinese  companies up until 2024 to comply so  there is still quite a bit of time left  and i'm not sure if 